  28:     """
  29:     Slide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.
  30: 
  31:     Input structure
  32:     - The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.
  33:     - Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.
  34: 
  35:     Rule
  36:     - Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.
  37:     - A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.
  38:     - A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.
  39:     - Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.
  40: 
  41:     Key insight
  42:     - Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.
  43:     """
  44:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  45:     assert g.ndim == 2
  46:     h, w = g.shape
  47:     assert h > 0 and w > 0
  48: 
  49:     moving = Color.BLACK
  50:     trail = Color.ORANGE
  51:     assert np.any(g == moving), "expected at least one black rectangle"
  52:     assert np.any(g == trail), "expected orange trail color to be present"
  53: 
  54:     out = g.copy()
  55:     targets: list[BBox] = []
  56:     for coords in components_mask(g == moving, connectivity=4):
  57:         r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(coords)
  58:         rect_h = r1 - r0 + 1
  59:         rect_w = c1 - c0 + 1
  60:         assert int(coords.shape[0]) == rect_h * rect_w, "black mask must be a solid rectangle"
  61: 
  62:         side = _edge_side((r0, c0, r1, c1), g.shape)
  63:         if side == "top":
  64:             out[:, c0 : c1 + 1] = trail
  65:             targets.append((h - rect_h, c0, h - 1, c1))
  66:         elif side == "bottom":
  67:             out[:, c0 : c1 + 1] = trail
  68:             targets.append((0, c0, rect_h - 1, c1))
  69:         elif side == "left":
  70:             out[r0 : r1 + 1, :] = trail
  71:             targets.append((r0, w - rect_w, r1, w - 1))
  72:         else:
  73:             assert side == "right"
  74:             out[r0 : r1 + 1, :] = trail
  75:             targets.append((r0, 0, r1, rect_w - 1))
  76: 
  77:     for r0, c0, r1, c1 in targets:
  78:         out[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1] = moving
